================================================================================
PART 2: UNDERSTANDING SIMPLE FORMS
================================================================================

WHAT IS A SIMPLE FORM?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A simple form can contain:

• One or more input fields

• State containing input values

• An onChange handler

• Controlled input values

• Labels and placeholders

• Optional live display of entered values


For this lesson:

• No advanced validation

• No API integration

• No real submission workflow

The focus is:

INPUT
  ↓
onChange
  ↓
STATE
  ↓
RENDERED VALUE


================================================================================
SIMPLE FORM CHARACTERISTICS
================================================================================

• Minimal complexity

• Clear structure

• Controlled input fields

• Single state object

• Shared change handler

• Easy to extend

• Easy to test

• Good foundation for complex forms


================================================================================
SIMPLE VS COMPLEX FORM
================================================================================

+----------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------------+
| ASPECT               | SIMPLE FORM           | COMPLEX FORM                  |
+----------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------------+
| Fields               | Few                   | Many                          |
| State                | Basic                 | More involved                 |
| Validation           | None/minimal          | Detailed                      |
| Error Handling       | Minimal               | Multiple cases                |
| Submission           | Basic/not included    | API/workflow driven           |
| Dependencies         | Minimal               | Fields may depend on others   |
| Complexity           | Low                   | Medium/High                   |
| Typical Purpose      | Learning/simple UI    | Production workflows          |
+----------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------------+


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Form complexity should be measured by behavior and requirements, not by
the number of lines in the component.


