4. NUMBER INPUT
================================================================================

<input
  type="number"
  name="age"
  value={formData.age}
  onChange={handleChange}
/>


IMPORTANT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

For regular DOM inputs:

event.target.value

is normally a string.

For example, typing:

25

into type="number" can still give:

"25"

through event.target.value.


Convert explicitly if your state should contain a number.

Example:

const parsedAge =
  event.target.value === ''
    ? ''
    : Number(event.target.value)


